<title>USA: Enron names Jeffrey Skilling president,COO.</title>
<headline>Enron names Jeffrey Skilling president,COO.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enron Corp said it named Jeffrey Skilling president and chief operating officer to replace Richard Kinder, who will resign at the end of the year to pursue other opportunities.</p>
<p>Skilling's new position is effective January 1, the company said.  He will also continue in his current position as chairman and chief executive of Enron Capital &amp; Trade Resources.</p>
<p>Skilling joined Enron in 1990. Kinder announced his intention to leave the company in November.</p>
